#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:101
#: b2f682d3d4fb4ac8a0508289646e1e6d
msgid "Landing Offset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:102
#: 38402a41b5534154a30c155ca837e17b
msgid "It is important to set the correct values for :ref:`FOLL_OFS_X<FOLL_OFS_X>`, :ref:`FOLL_OFS_Y<FOLL_OFS_Y>` and :ref:`FOLL_OFS_Z<FOLL_OFS_Z>` on the aircraft for the landing point relative to the beacon. These values are in meters, in front-right-down format. The easiest way to set these is to place the aircraft in the correct landing location with the beacon working and then set the parameter ``SHIP_AUTO_OFS`` to 1. When this parameter is set to 1 then the ship landing lua script will calculate the right offset values and set them in the :ref:`FOLL_OFS_X<FOLL_OFS_X>`, :ref:`FOLL_OFS_Y<FOLL_OFS_Y>` and :ref:`FOLL_OFS_Z<FOLL_OFS_Z>` values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:105
#: 02c5c5bdab744b438c127834bea5d30c
msgid "The values are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:107
#: 790c3b70235542e6a5f924e5d5bc1ba7
msgid ":ref:`FOLL_OFS_X<FOLL_OFS_X>` distance in front of the beacon to land (use a negative value for landing behind the beacon)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:108
#: 3d1b73400d104050975e01cec0ecdb92
msgid ":ref:`FOLL_OFS_Y<FOLL_OFS_Y>` distance to the right of the beacon to land (use a negative value for left)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:109
#: 9d90bbb487be4d54b7d6c84b0fa425a6
msgid ":ref:`FOLL_OFS_Z<FOLL_OFS_Z>` distance below the beacon to land (use a negative value to land above the beacon)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:111
#: 871dc0efb75f4e0592af533c73d690be
msgid "When the beacon is active you should see the HOME icon on the GCS move to match the landing position. The HOME position is continuously updated while you are flying which gives you a good way to ensure that the beacon is working properly before you land."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:113
#: 7fc6d9d9cc0244b7808b9a8e3ddc5748
msgid "It is recommended that the method of setting ``SHIP_AUTO_OFS`` = 1 is used to get the location before each flight. Look carefully at the message it gives when this parameter is set(use the Messages tab in MissionPlanner):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:115
#: 6879fe39d06f4aa1978e82fc6565220c
msgid "Set follow offset (-10.82,3.29,0.46)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:117
#: 9c128fec2559481796206d0677add9ae
msgid "That message confirms that the X, Y and Z offset has calculated. Check that they are reasonable, paying close attention to the Z offset. If you get a bad Z offset (ie. a long way off from the actual height difference between the beacon and the aircraft) then you may need to reboot the beacon and/or aircraft to cope with GPS altitude drift."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:120
#: 37ecd52c18da4c1eaa2fdaf5d51b9d9c
msgid "Takeoff Procedure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:121
#: 742a247fe43242f0907ecab8a6d6a68d
msgid "When ``SHIP_ENABLE`` = 1 and the beacon is visible to the aircraft then an AUTO VTOL takeoff will use velocity matching, so the aircraft will hold its velocity relative to the beacon while ascending. This velocity matching is only done for VTOL takeoff as a mission item in AUTO mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:124
#: 49f1017eb76f4f719eeb2be0a8f47dae
msgid "Hold-off Position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:125
#: d908b7a4095f49fda9a4f2e6bf6be9df
msgid "A key part of ship landing is the “hold-off position”. The hold-off position is where the aircraft will loiter while waiting for the pilot to command the landing via the movement of the throttle stick (see throttle stick information below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:127
#: 88690b131fef4a61997efed05559d278
msgid "The holdoff position is based on a few criteria:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:129
#: 8c878aea197245efb5f8da5368aea521
msgid ":ref:`RTL_RADIUS<RTL_RADIUS>` in meters (negative for counter-clockwise loiter, positive for clockwise loiter). If :ref:`RTL_RADIUS<RTL_RADIUS>` is zero, then the :ref:`WP_LOITER_RAD<WP_LOITER_RAD>` parameter is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:130
#: 6b8bf9b12db7480cac1bf08c3728de04
msgid "``SHIP_LAND_ANGLE`` parameter, which controls the angle that the aircraft will approach the ship for landing. A value of zero means to approach from behind the ship. The hold-off loiter position will be setup so that the tangent of the circle intercepts the beacon landing point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:131
#: c088c1b71e1445f9be0c20b76fe0810d
msgid ":ref:`Q_TRANS_DECEL<Q_TRANS_DECEL>` parameter, which determines how fast the aircraft can slow down"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:132
#: 0c05c7e42bbe4a88b5a91c7bff3b9bc6
msgid "The speed of the ship, the wind speed and the speed of the aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:134
#: 63eebef8bed742c4ab522de495234ea2
msgid "Here is an example where ``SHIP_LAND_ANGLE`` is -45 and :ref:`RTL_RADIUS<RTL_RADIUS>` is -100:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:138
#: 2f3b9bf67f47431c9abe8ac74071b417
msgid "and here is an example with ``SHIP_LAND_ANGLE`` at 0 and :ref:`RTL_RADIUS<RTL_RADIUS>` at 100:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:143
#: 94c7f885d4d649eda2c10b64ed7a3450
msgid "Landing Procedure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:144
#: b621a4e373c847a0aade74c3fc0c0acd
msgid "When you are ready to land you can switch the vehicle to RTL mode. When in RTL mode the aircraft will fly towards the landing location (you can see this location before you land from the HOME icon on the GCS, which moves with the beacon)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:146
#: f55dfca6c4ef4be2871225ed2275d981
msgid "The aircraft will initially approach the “hold-off” position. The altitude of the holdoff position is set by the :ref:`RTL_ALTITUDE<RTL_ALTITUDE>` parameter (in centimeters above the landing location). A good value of this is around 9000, which is 90 meters above the landing location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:148
#: e5dc341ce67a479bacfc2c4eddaf6801
msgid "The description below will assume that ``SHIP_LAND_ANGLE`` = 0 which means landing happens from behind the beacon. The approach and landing is rotated by the value of this parameter in degrees. With ``SHIP_LAND_ANGLE`` = 0, the hold-off position will be behind and above the beacon. The distance depends on the beacon speed, wind speed and the :ref:`Q_TRANS_DECEL<Q_TRANS_DECEL>` parameter (which controls the deceleration of the aircraft)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:151
#: b295d632ed524db9a16ebbc51a71ab7e
msgid "Once the aircraft arrives at the hold-off position it will circle until the throttle stick is lowered below 40%. The throttle stick on the transmitter is used to control the landing sequence and also to abort the landing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:153
#: 059616f5d9334430931e44cc38c45e68
msgid "Throttle stick controls are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:155
#: 0e452737858e4e75b0508223599255bb
msgid "Throttle at 40% or above means to hold at the hold-off position (at :ref:`RTL_ALTITUDE<RTL_ALTITUDE>` height above beacon in centimeters)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:156
#: b0fca4b26722487b89c97d98fdcf61fc
msgid "Throttle below 40% and above 10% means to descend while loitering to the approach altitude. The approach altitude is giving by :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>` in meters above the beacon. A good value for testing may be 40 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:157
#: d908d230841b433ab40f41ccdf920e41
msgid "Throttle below 10% means to start landing approach once the aircraft is at the :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>` and lined up with the ``SHIP_LAND_ANGLE`` to move toward the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:159
#: 8fdfdafd66394f74890a9bed6c6acf76
msgid "Once the landing descent has started can still abort the landing. To do this, the :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 15 must be set to enable ThrLandControl. When that option is set you can raise the throttle momentarily above 70% to enable throttle control for climb and descent rate. You can use this to slow the descent or climb back up. If you climb up past the :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>` approach altitude then the aircraft will go back to loitering at the hold-off location at :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:161
#: b2df1c9767e14688b67567a226fc280d
msgid "You may also want to enable horizontal repositioning with the :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 17(EnableLandResponsition). If that is enabled then you can manually reposition the aircraft horizontally while landing to account for any GPS position errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:164
#: 122be5e369114e57b439e66975e70f70
msgid "Simple Mission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:165
#: 1f151c20b12b4cfd87f30438e64f1c71
msgid "The simplest mission would be a single VTOL_TAKEOFF waypoint. Once the takeoff is complete the aircraft will immediately switch to RTL mode and go to the hold-off location. You should have the throttle stick above 40% to keep the aircraft circling at the hold-off location. This very simple mission is good for ship operations as it does not have specific latitude/longitude, so will work wherever the ship is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ship-landing.rst:167
#: 8679be29de94489da6b2e7f1a482f7ae
msgid "You could also switch to a fixed wing mode just before reaching the takeoff altitude you set, then fly under pilot control and when ready to land, simply switch back into AUTO to RTL and land."
msgstr ""

